{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nYou are given three positive integers x,\u2009y,\u2009n. Your task is to find the nearest fraction to fraction  whose denominator is no more than n. Formally, you should find such pair of integers a,\u2009b (1\u2009\u2264\u2009b\u2009\u2264\u2009n;\u00a00\u2009\u2264\u2009a) that the value  is as minimal as possible.If there are multiple \"nearest\" fractions, choose the one with the minimum denominator. If there are multiple \"nearest\" fractions with the minimum denominator, choose the one with the minimum numerator.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++17 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <set>\n#include <tuple>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <numeric>\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\ni64 compute_gcd(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    for (i64 t; b != 0; t = b, b = a % b, a = t);\n    return a;\n}\n\ni64 compute_ceil_div(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    return (a + b - 1) / b;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    i64 x, y, n;\n    std::cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    std::set<std::pair<i64, i64>> fraction_set;\n    \n    for (i64 i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        i64 lower = (x * i) / y;\n        i64 upper = compute_ceil_div(x * i, y);\n        \n        if ((lower + upper) * y > 2 * x * i) {\n            i64 g = compute_gcd(i, lower);\n            fraction_set.emplace(i / g, lower / g);\n        } else {\n            i64 g = compute_gcd(i, upper);\n            fraction_set.emplace(i / g, upper / g);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    auto best = *fraction_set.begin();\n    \n    for (const auto& [q, p] : fraction_set) {\n        i64 current = p * y;\n        i64 expected = x * q;\n        \n        if (current == expected) {\n            best = {q, p};\n        } else if (current > expected) {\n            if (best.second * y > x * best.first) {\n                if (p * best.first < best.second * q) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            } else {\n                if (2 * x * best.first * q > y * (best.second * q + best.first * p)) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (best.second * y > x * best.first) {\n                if (2 * x * best.first * q < y * (best.second * q + best.first * p)) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            } else {\n                if (p * best.first > best.second * q) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    i64 g = compute_gcd(best.first, best.second);\n    std::cout << best.second / g << '/' << best.first / g << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <set>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdlib>\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\ni64 compute_gcd(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    for (i64 t; b != 0; t = b, b = a % b, a = t);\n    return a;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    i64 x, y, n;\n    std::cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    i64 best_a = 0, best_b = 1;\n    i64 min_diff = LLONG_MAX;\n    \n    for (i64 b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n        // Find the best numerator a for denominator b\n        // We want a/b \u2248 x/y, so a \u2248 (x*b)/y\n        i64 a = (x * b) / y;\n        \n        // Check both floor and ceil candidates\n        for (i64 candidate_a : {a, a+1}) {\n            if (candidate_a < 0) continue;\n            \n            // Compute absolute difference |candidate_a/b - x/y|\n            // Use cross multiplication to avoid floating point: |candidate_a*y - x*b| / (b*y)\n            i64 diff = std::abs(candidate_a * y - x * b);\n            \n            // Compare with current best\n            // We want minimal diff, then minimal b, then minimal candidate_a\n            i64 current_diff_b = diff * best_b;\n            i64 best_diff_b = std::abs(best_a * y - x * best_b) * b;\n            \n            if (current_diff_b < best_diff_b ||\n                (current_diff_b == best_diff_b && b < best_b) ||\n                (current_diff_b == best_diff_b && b == best_b && candidate_a < best_a)) {\n                best_a = candidate_a;\n                best_b = b;\n                min_diff = diff;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Simplify the fraction\n    i64 g = compute_gcd(best_a, best_b);\n    std::cout << best_a / g << '/' << best_b / g << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.9073468138230965e-06, -6.317892984952778e-05, -5.483612312673358e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.483612312673358e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.6600162982940674, -6.198863957251888e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -0.41195443272590637, -5.2927523938706145e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0